.Dd 24 July 2026
.Dt SPIDER_ID 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm spider_id
.Nd compute radiopharmaceutical administration identifier
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm spider_id
.Op Fl Vv
.Ar directory
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
computes a radiopharmaceutical administration identifier from the
DICOM series in
.Ar directory ,
which is expected to have SOP Class Positron Emission Tomography Image
Storage.  The identifier is printed to the standard output.
.Pp
The identifier has the form
.Dq <NAME>--<ID>__<RADIONUCLIDE>++<START DATETIME> ,
where the fields have the following values, except that the characters
space,
.Ql / ,
.Ql < ,
.Ql > ,
.Ql \&: ,
.Ql \(dq ,
.Ql \e ,
.Ql | ,
.Ql ?\& ,
and
.Ql *
are omitted:
.Bl -tag -width "<START DATETIME>"
.It <NAME>
The value of the DICOM attribute Patient's Name (0010,0010).
.It <ID>
The value of the DICOM attribute Patient ID (0010,0020).
.It <RADIONUCLIDE>
The value of the DICOM attribute Code Meaning (0008,0104) in the
Radionuclide Code Sequence (0054,0300).
.It <START DATETIME>
The value of the DICOM attribute Radiopharmaceutical Start DateTime
(0018,1078), but with the first period and any following characters
omitted.
.El
.Pp
If an attribute is absent, the corresponding field is empty.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl V
Display the version number and exit.
.Pp
.It Fl v
Verbose mode.  Causes
.Nm
to print debugging messages about its progress.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr spider 1
